---
// Expandable 4-layer architecture stack diagram
// Layer order: 4 (top/applications) → 3 → 2 → 1 (bottom/integration)
---

<div class="arch-diagram" role="list" aria-label="Intelligence Fabric architecture layers">

  <!-- Layer 4 — Domain Agent Applications (top) -->
  <div class="arch-layer layer-4" role="listitem">
    <button class="layer-header" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="layer-4-detail">
      <div class="layer-meta">
        <span class="layer-num">Layer 4</span>
        <div class="layer-domain-badges">
          <span class="domain-badge cx">CX Agents</span>
          <span class="domain-badge finops">FinOps Agents</span>
          <span class="domain-badge grc">GRC Agents</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="layer-title-row">
        <h3 class="layer-title">Domain Agent Applications</h3>
        <span class="layer-expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/>
          </svg>
        </span>
      </div>
      <p class="layer-summary">
        Six domain-specific agent types operating across CX, FinOps, and GRC applications.
      </p>
    </button>
    <div class="layer-detail" id="layer-4-detail" hidden>
      <p>
        Six domain-specific agent types operate across the three platform applications: Patient
        Engagement, Care Continuity, RCM Optimisation, Supply Intelligence, GRC Compliance, and
        Analytics &amp; Insights. Each agent is configured against validated operational bottlenecks
        identified during the audit phase.
      </p>
      <div class="agent-chips">
        <span class="agent-chip cx-chip">Patient Engagement Agent</span>
        <span class="agent-chip cx-chip">Care Continuity Agent</span>
        <span class="agent-chip finops-chip">RCM Optimisation Agent</span>
        <span class="agent-chip finops-chip">Supply Intelligence Agent</span>
        <span class="agent-chip grc-chip">GRC Compliance Agent</span>
        <span class="agent-chip cross-chip">Analytics &amp; Insights Agent</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="layer-connector" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="connector-line"></div>
    <div class="connector-arrow">↓</div>
  </div>

  <!-- Layer 3 — Agent Platform Core -->
  <div class="arch-layer layer-3" role="listitem">
    <button class="layer-header" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="layer-3-detail">
      <div class="layer-meta">
        <span class="layer-num">Layer 3</span>
        <span class="layer-badge platform-badge">Intelligence Fabric Core</span>
      </div>
      <div class="layer-title-row">
        <h3 class="layer-title">Agent Platform</h3>
        <span class="layer-expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/>
          </svg>
        </span>
      </div>
      <p class="layer-summary">
        Orchestration · HITL governance · Self-learning · LLM observability · Cost-aware routing
      </p>
    </button>
    <div class="layer-detail" id="layer-3-detail" hidden>
      <p>
        The core of the platform: the agent runtime, orchestration layer, and human-in-the-loop
        governance framework. Key capabilities:
      </p>
      <ul class="layer-list">
        <li><strong>Agent lifecycle management</strong> — deploy, monitor, retrain, and retire agents systematically</li>
        <li><strong>Multi-agent orchestration</strong> — agents that coordinate across domains (e.g., a care gap agent triggering a follow-up agent)</li>
        <li><strong>Human-in-the-loop (HITL) governance</strong> — every agent has defined confidence thresholds and impact boundaries above which a human must confirm</li>
        <li><strong>Self-learning (RLHF/GEPA)</strong> — agents improve from operational feedback, exception analysis, and outcome data</li>
        <li><strong>LLM observability</strong> — full visibility into model behaviour, prompt performance, and output quality</li>
        <li><strong>Cost-aware model execution</strong> — task-specific model routing to balance accuracy and cost</li>
        <li><strong>Conversational mode</strong> — natural language query across operational data cubes, beyond fixed dashboards</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="layer-connector" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="connector-line"></div>
    <div class="connector-arrow">↓</div>
  </div>

  <!-- Layer 2 — Domain Data Foundation -->
  <div class="arch-layer layer-2" role="listitem">
    <button class="layer-header" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="layer-2-detail">
      <div class="layer-meta">
        <span class="layer-num">Layer 2</span>
      </div>
      <div class="layer-title-row">
        <h3 class="layer-title">Domain Data Foundation</h3>
        <span class="layer-expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/>
          </svg>
        </span>
      </div>
      <p class="layer-summary">
        Clinical cubes · Financial cubes · Operational cubes · Cross-domain federation
      </p>
    </button>
    <div class="layer-detail" id="layer-2-detail" hidden>
      <p>
        Raw system data is cleaned, normalised, and structured into domain-specific data cubes —
        clinical, financial, operational. Governed metric definitions. Historical and real-time views.
        Cross-domain federation for workflows that span departments. This is the factual foundation
        agents reason over.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="layer-connector" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="connector-line"></div>
    <div class="connector-arrow">↓</div>
  </div>

  <!-- Layer 1 — Integration & Data (bottom) -->
  <div class="arch-layer layer-1" role="listitem">
    <button class="layer-header" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="layer-1-detail">
      <div class="layer-meta">
        <span class="layer-num">Layer 1</span>
        <div class="system-badges">
          <span class="sys-badge">EMR / EHR</span>
          <span class="sys-badge">HIS</span>
          <span class="sys-badge">HL7</span>
          <span class="sys-badge">FHIR</span>
          <span class="sys-badge">REST API</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="layer-title-row">
        <h3 class="layer-title">Integration &amp; Data</h3>
        <span class="layer-expand-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/>
          </svg>
        </span>
      </div>
      <p class="layer-summary">
        HL7 · FHIR · REST API · File ingestion · EMR, HIS, and payer portal connectors
      </p>
    </button>
    <div class="layer-detail" id="layer-1-detail" hidden>
      <p>
        The Intelligence Fabric connects to your existing systems via HL7, FHIR, HL7 v2, REST API,
        or flat file. Pre-built connectors for major EMR, HIS, CRM, and SCM platforms. File, API,
        and CDC ingestion. Real-time and batch pipelines. Your data stays in your environment.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<style>
  .arch-diagram {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    width: 100%;
  }

  /* Layers */
  .arch-layer {
    border: 1px solid var(--diagram-border);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--diagram-bg);
    transition: border-color 0.3s ease;
  }

  .arch-layer:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-default);
  }

  .arch-layer.is-open {
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
  }

  /* Layer-specific accent tops */
  .layer-4 { border-top: 2px solid var(--domain-cx); }
  .layer-3 { border-top: 2px solid var(--accent-primary); }
  .layer-2 { border-top: 2px solid var(--domain-finops); }
  .layer-1 { border-top: 2px solid var(--domain-grc); }

  /* Header button */
  .layer-header {
    width: 100%;
    text-align: left;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    color: inherit;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .layer-header:hover {
    background: var(--bg-highlight);
  }

  .layer-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .layer-num {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .layer-title-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .layer-title {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .layer-expand-icon {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
    display: flex;
  }

  .arch-layer.is-open .layer-expand-icon {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .layer-summary {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* Domain badges */
  .layer-domain-badges {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.375rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .domain-badge {
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid;
  }

  .domain-badge.cx {
    color: var(--domain-cx);
    background: var(--domain-cx-muted);
    border-color: var(--domain-cx-border);
  }

  .domain-badge.finops {
    color: var(--domain-finops);
    background: var(--domain-finops-muted);
    border-color: var(--domain-finops-border);
  }

  .domain-badge.grc {
    color: var(--domain-grc);
    background: var(--domain-grc-muted);
    border-color: var(--domain-grc-border);
  }

  /* Platform badge */
  .layer-badge {
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .platform-badge {
    color: var(--accent-primary);
    background: var(--bg-highlight);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  /* System badges */
  .system-badges {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.375rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .sys-badge {
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    background: var(--bg-highlight);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  /* Detail panel */
  .layer-detail {
    padding: 0 1.5rem 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .layer-detail p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
  }

  .layer-list {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0 0;
    padding: 0 0 0 1rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .layer-list li {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .layer-list li strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  /* Agent chips inside detail */
  .agent-chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .agent-chip {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    border: 1px solid;
  }

  .cx-chip {
    color: var(--domain-cx);
    background: var(--domain-cx-muted);
    border-color: var(--domain-cx-border);
  }

  .finops-chip {
    color: var(--domain-finops);
    background: var(--domain-finops-muted);
    border-color: var(--domain-finops-border);
  }

  .grc-chip {
    color: var(--domain-grc);
    background: var(--domain-grc-muted);
    border-color: var(--domain-grc-border);
  }

  .cross-chip {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    background: var(--bg-highlight);
    border-color: var(--border-subtle);
  }

  /* Connectors between layers */
  .layer-connector {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0;
    padding: 0;
    position: relative;
  }

  .connector-line {
    width: 1px;
    height: 20px;
    background: var(--layer-connector);
  }

  .connector-arrow {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-top: -2px;
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Toggle expand/collapse for each layer
  document.querySelectorAll('.arch-layer .layer-header').forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const layer = btn.closest('.arch-layer') as HTMLElement;
      const detailId = btn.getAttribute('aria-controls');
      const detail = detailId ? document.getElementById(detailId) : null;
      const isOpen = btn.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';

      btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!isOpen));
      if (detail) detail.hidden = isOpen;
      layer.classList.toggle('is-open', !isOpen);
    });
  });
</script>
